WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:02.348
Yikes!

2
00:00:02.349 --> 00:00:04.949
Who

3
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:08.291
are you? I'm

4
00:00:08.292 --> 00:00:12.003
an American alligator. Alligators

5
00:00:12.004 --> 00:00:16.557
are large reptiles. Where

6
00:00:16.558 --> 00:00:19.287
do you live? We

7
00:00:19.288 --> 00:00:23.243
live in the United States. We

8
00:00:23.244 --> 00:00:26.364
like warm water. We

9
00:00:26.365 --> 00:00:31.418
swim in rivers, lakes, and swamps. What

10
00:00:31.419 --> 00:00:34.408
do you eat? We

11
00:00:34.409 --> 00:00:39.403
like frogs, fish, snails, and mammals. Alligators

12
00:00:39.404 --> 00:00:43.044
don't chew food. We

13
00:00:43.045 --> 00:00:49.727
just gulp it down! You

14
00:00:49.728 --> 00:00:53.208
have wide jaws. My

15
00:00:53.209 --> 00:00:57.477
jaws are very strong. I

16
00:00:57.478 --> 00:01:03.043
can even crack a turtle's hard shell! We

17
00:01:03.044 --> 00:01:08.968
grab prey with our sharp teeth.

18
00:01:08.969 --> 00:01:12.657
This swamp is noisy!

19
00:01:12.658 --> 00:01:17.820
Alligators hiss loudly.

20
00:01:17.821 --> 00:01:24.817
We can roar like lions too.

21
00:01:24.818 --> 00:01:27.968
Do you hibernate?

22
00:01:27.969 --> 00:01:32.406
No. But we sleep in holes sometimes.

23
00:01:32.407 --> 00:01:36.289
We find a muddy spot in water.

24
00:01:36.290 --> 00:01:40.525
Then we dig holes to keep warm.

25
00:01:40.526 --> 00:01:44.564
Your tail looks powerful!

26
00:01:44.565 --> 00:01:47.676
It is powerful.

27
00:01:47.677 --> 00:01:51.756
My tail moves me through the water.

28
00:01:51.757 --> 00:01:57.483
I love to swim.

29
00:01:57.484 --> 00:02:00.819
I'm getting hungry.

30
00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:04.389
Bye.

31
00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:11.360
See you later, American Alligator!

